                        "glosses": [
                            "Able to be expected.",
                            "Able to be expected or anticipated; not unusual."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c861ec6-8258-4fb1-bc17-48711fa94167",
                                "sense_id": "cae44c29-076e-3e3e-8dc2-671eb12309fd",
                                "text": "Expectable losses are calculated into the final selling price."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ef8fe77-69bf-32a8-b347-4edef5c83ae9",
                        "entry_id": "d70ba861-0f39-35f4-8186-3322b6b57aaa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Able to be expected.",
                            "Able to be expected or considered due or required (of someone), reasonable to expect (someone to do, have, etc)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "568df4c7-336d-4fb9-a5bf-2e82f6fd4715",
                                "sense_id": "1ef8fe77-69bf-32a8-b347-4edef5c83ae9",
                                "text": "The jury could and did find that appellant's decision not to move was not a decision expectable of a reasonably prudent man to whom any backing vehicle means grave danger."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2074c321-a7f0-4c82-b0b2-8d7ceff747aa",
                                "sense_id": "1ef8fe77-69bf-32a8-b347-4edef5c83ae9",
                                "text": "An argument can be made that the Marquesan view of certain states as expectable of 'persons' follows from these being equally examples of a common type of process."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8785c26-6ed9-46ba-82aa-110930892242",
                                "sense_id": "1ef8fe77-69bf-32a8-b347-4edef5c83ae9",
                                "text": "And that is the tragedy of the establishment of the diagnosis of PTSD. The presence of troubling war-related memories and associated negative reactions typically has much more to do with what is normal and expectable of almost anyone who has survived war ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a61afa1-5e39-4a77-bfae-2467c2869c04",
                                "sense_id": "1ef8fe77-69bf-32a8-b347-4edef5c83ae9",
                                "text": "Such issues finally turn on two counts; namely, what is most opposite to the human scene, and what is most properly worth, or—may we say— “expectable” of God."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
